"q": "What is the primary purpose of US GAAP?",
"a": "<p>In the US, the SEC delegates the job of setting accounting rules for public companies to the Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB).</p><p>FASB requires financial statements to be prepared under US Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (US GAAP).</p><p>The point is standardisation: if every company reports on the same fair, consistent basis, investors and lenders can rely on and compare the numbers — which is how GAAP protects their interests.</p>",
