"a": "<p><b>Income statement (IS):</b> shows profitability over a period, usually a quarter or a year. It starts with revenue, deducts costs and expenses, and ends at net income.</p><p><b>Balance sheet (BS):</b> a snapshot at one point in time (e.g. quarter- or year-end) of what the company has — its assets — and how those assets were funded — liabilities and shareholders’ equity.</p><p><b>Cash flow statement (CFS):</b> under the indirect method it starts from net income, adjusts for non-cash items like D&amp;A and for changes in working capital to get cash from operations, then adds cash from investing and cash from financing. The total is the net change in cash — the actual cash inflow or outflow for the period.</p>",
