"q": "Which is more important, the income statement or the cash flow statement?",
"a": "<p>You need both for any proper analysis. But the cash flow statement has the stronger claim to being more important: it reconciles net income — the accrual-based bottom line — back to what actually happened to cash.</p><p>Because the CFS records the real movement of cash in the period, it exposes liquidity problems, as well as investing and financing activity, that never appear on the accrual-based income statement.</p>",
