"q": "When do you capitalize vs. expense items under accrual accounting?",
"a": "<p>It comes down to the item’s <b>useful life</b> — how long the benefits are expected to last.</p><p><b>Capitalise:</b> spending on fixed and intangible assets expected to benefit the company for more than a year is recorded as an asset and expensed gradually. A building, for instance, might provide benefits for 15+ years, so it is depreciated over that useful life.</p><p><b>Expense:</b> when the benefit is short-term, the cost is expensed in the period it’s incurred. Inventory turns over within the year, and wages are expensed when the employee provides the work.</p>",
